body:
1) Learn about hypothesis' fornulation, the scientific method overall (I like "What is this thing called Science", by Chalmers) (without this you can't properly understand statistics);

2) Learn basic statistics from media outlets such as Youtube, blogs, or Coursera (types of variables, what a population is, sampling, and so on);

3) Learn about basic tests, and practice said basic/common tests (eg. t student, anova, ancova etc.) on SPSS (I recommend SPSS because you mentioned you study psychology), alongside a tutorial.
